in @prism
in @mirror/cli
in @mirror/mosaic
in @pack
in @magic
in @magic/contract
in @spectral/supervisor

# @mirror/pack — the `pack { }` block substrate-decl in `mirror.spec`.
#
# The substrate-altitude grammar for the lambda-shell-counterparty +
# ACL surface that `docs/specs/mirror-spec-peer-acl-surface.md`
# ratifies. Mirror provides the BLOCK SHAPE; consumers ship their
# specific pack INSTANCES at their own `mirror.spec` (substrate-vs-USE
# distinction; spec §7.4 + Alex 2026-06-24).
#
# === What @mirror/pack IS ===
#
# The substrate-decl that names `pack { lead ~peer'<home>' bindings
# { … } members { ~peer'<home>' => <acl>, … } }` as a typed surface
# in mirror.spec. Lifts the block from "text the parser handles" to
# "prism the substrate types." Discharges peer-ACL spec §3.3's
# forward-promise; closes peer-ACL Phase C of the LOCAL-PACK loop;
# composes with @spectral/supervisor at runtime altitude (peer-ACL
# §2.4); composes with @pack's existing `peer` variant (peer-ACL
# §3.3 reuse rule).
#
# === Why now ===
#
# Slingshot tick per Taut scout 2026-06-24 (`docs/scouts/2026-06-24-
# taut-substrate-pull-scout.md` §2): landing this shard closes Phase
# C, dissolves peer-ACL §2.4 hedge (`in @spectral/supervisor`
# composition typechecks against the existing glass declaration at
# `shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror:322`), and unblocks the
# downstream phases (peer identity-substrate loader; @mirror/spawn
# refinement; the mirror MCP `mirror_spawn` Phase G).
#
# Substrate-pull-confidence HIGH per Taut; landed by Reed per
# established Pack-altitude review chain (Mara wrote, Seam verified,
# Taut scouted, Reed lands).
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - #84 (@pack multi-repo agent runtime; promoted): the `peer`
#   variant + `spawn` primitive at substrate floor. This shard's
#   `lead` and `members` fields reuse @pack's `peer`. Named-peer
#   instances are transitional per Alex 2026-06-24; the @pack carrier
#   substrate-decl is permanent at mirror altitude.
# - #58 (Fate IS optical inference; promoted): the substrate's
#   inference primitive. No `@io/llm` adapter; the pack{}-block
#   resolution + lambda-shell counterparty work over Fate.
# - #53 (composed-bilateral; promoted): the predicate-discipline
#   pattern. Forward-promised bilateral `pack_block_coherent` will
#   compose `lead_well_formed` + `members_well_formed` + ACL
#   discipline; not landed in this tick (peer-ACL §3.3 ratifies the
#   shape only).
# - geometric-consent-projection (Reed memory; type-1 projection):
#   the ACL substrate. The `but` operator + `∨` / `∧` lattice ops
#   are inherited from the consent spec; no new ACL algebra here.
#
# === The substrate-vs-USE rule (Alex 2026-06-24) ===
#
# Mirror ships the block SHAPE (this file). Consumers ship pack
# INSTANCES. mirror.spec for the mirror project itself will eventually
# carry a `pack { lead ~peer'~/.reed' members { … } }` block; that
# block is Alex/Reed's pack at the USE altitude, not mirror's default
# substrate. The empty-pack-default rule (peer-ACL §9) governs the
# absence case.
#
# === The lambda-shell counterparty rule (peer-ACL §4) ===
#
# The `lead` field names the peer who answers when a human opens the
# lambda shell at this spec's root, AND who fields the spectral-Tomm-
# shaped circular probes lifting from spawned members (per peer-ACL
# §10 reframe; lead is N+1 OBSERVER, not delegation chain). This
# substrate-decl ratifies the shape; runtime discharge composes with
# @spectral/supervisor (above) + @magic/contract.honor + @magic/audit
# at the audit-time evaluation pass.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art (peer-ACL §3 discovery) ===
#
# Seven existing substrate shapes Mara surfaced: `peer = @<name>`
# per-spec declaration (lambda-shell.md); `@peer` glass (peer-glass.
# md); `@pack` variant + `pack_coherent`; `@spectral/supervisor`
# with restart_strategy; `@magic/{contract,audit,reveal}`; geometric-
# consent-projection; the `~git'…'` sigil precedent. The pack{} block
# unifies these under one surface plus three new rules (self-naming;
# lexical scope; default-to-repo-local).

prism @mirror/pack {
  focus mirror_pack_block
  project mirror_pack_block
  split mirror_pack_block
  shift mirror_pack_block
  settle mirror_pack_block
}

# === The acl carrier ===
#
# Parametric ref; refined at species per peer-ACL §5. The acl literal
# (forward-promised type at the @mirror/peer grammar) carries three
# substrate-typed slots: `ops` (the five operations + the @magic
# operation family); `targets` (paths + content-address prefixes +
# prism-name prefixes per O5 still-open); `predicates` (the @magic-
# style verdict carrier). The slot-grammar lands when O5 settles.
#
# Composition rules (per peer-ACL §10):
#
#   - The `but` operator (geometric-consent-projection §2.4):
#     not commutative, not associative, monotone in default.
#     `writer but(exception: target_under(~d'.secret/'))` means
#     "writer EXCEPT for targets under .secret/." Forecloses XACML's
#     combining-algorithm-zoo (consent spec §5.7): ONE composition
#     rule, not seven.
#   - The lattice operators ∨ (join) and ∧ (meet): bounded lattice
#     (⊥ = no_access; ⊤ = full_access); distributive on `ops` and
#     `targets` axes independently, non-distributive at the
#     `predicates` axis (the structural reason @magic/contract.honor
#     exists as a separate operational check rather than collapsing
#     into lattice algebra — peer-ACL §10.2 finding).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type acl = ref

# === The identifier carrier ===
#
# A let-binding name bound to an acl value at the bindings slot.
# Used for ACL reuse: `let read_only = acl { … }` then
# `members { ~peer'~/.glint' => read_only }`. Reuses the
# substrate's existing expression grammar; no new lexer rule.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type identifier = ref

# === The mirror_pack_block carrier ===
#
# The typed carrier for the parsed `pack { … }` block. Three fields:
#
#   lead     — the lambda-shell counterparty + spawn-and-probe N+1
#              observer. REQUIRED iff pack{} is present at all
#              (peer-ACL §3.3); absent pack{} triggers the default-
#              to-repo-local rule (§9).
#
#   bindings — the `let <identifier> = <acl>` declarations within
#              the bindings sub-block. List of (identifier, acl)
#              pairs; substrate-typed as `ref` until the substrate's
#              tuple-list carrier surfaces at @epistemologic altitude
#              (forward-promised).
#
#   members  — the `members { ~peer'…' => <acl>, … }` map. List of
#              (peer, acl) pairs; OPTIONAL (a spec with `lead` only
#              is admissible — the lead is the sole peer with
#              infinite ACL per peer-ACL §3.3).
#
# `peer` is reused from @pack (recognition #84). The lead must be a
# pack peer (substrate-vs-USE caveat: the @pack `peer` variant is
# transitional per Alex 2026-06-24; when the variant goes parametric,
# this shard's `lead: peer` annotation broadens correspondingly
# without surface change).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the (lead, bindings, members)
# triple.
type mirror_pack_block = {
  lead:     peer,
  bindings: ref,
  members:  ref,
}

# === Forward-promised — NOT landed this tick ===
#
# Per peer-ACL §3.3 + spec discipline (H1 ratifies SHAPE; discharge
# is multi-tick):
#
#   - parse(text: ref, p: perturbation) -> imperfect(mirror_pack_block, ref, ref)
#     The parser action that lifts source text → typed block.
#     Discharges through @mirror/mosaic at settle altitude.
#
#   - resolve_peer(p: peer, p: perturbation) -> imperfect(peer, ref, ref)
#     The self-naming-rule resolver (peer-ACL §6.2 + O7 dissolved):
#     ONE filesystem lookup (\<path>/mirror.spec) + ONE optional
#     pack{}-block read returns the peer's self-declared identity.
#     No transitive chase.
#
#   - admit(b: mirror_pack_block, pe: peer, op: operation, t: target, p: perturbation)
#       -> verdict
#     The ACL admission discharge (peer-ACL §5.4): walks members for
#     `pe`; evaluates the matching acl's ops/targets/predicates
#     against (op, t); returns the verdict carrier per @magic/audit.
#
#   - pack_block_coherent(b: mirror_pack_block, p: perturbation) -> verdict
#     Composed bilateral per recognition #53 family (12+ altitude
#     lifts). Composes:
#       lead_well_formed(b.lead, p)
#       ∧ members_well_formed(b.members, p)
#       ∧ bindings_well_formed(b.bindings, p)
#       ∧ acl_lattice_consistent(b, p)
#     Lands when the parser + admission discharge land (gates on the
#     sub-bilaterals existing as substrate-decl).
#
# These actions are NAMED here as forward-promise anchor; their
# bodies are discharged in subsequent ticks (peer-ACL §13 H1).

out @mirror/pack
out acl
out identifier
out mirror_pack_block
